The Responses-to-Chat conversion design is informed by codex-deepseek-proxy
(MIT License, copyright 2026 Codex DeepSeek Proxy Contributors):
https://github.com/himmetozcan/codex-deepseek-proxy

The implementation in this repository was rewritten for the PCL Tailnet
gateway, adds model discovery, a dependency-free MCP server, client installers,
workspace locking, and Codex subprocess delegation.

The unified provider/model routing, Codex-home ownership journal, health
surface, and dashboard information architecture were also informed by
OpenCodex (MIT License, copyright 2026 opencodex contributors):
https://github.com/lidge-jun/opencodex

PCL Relay keeps a narrower personal-Tailnet scope: it does not import or
manage the user's OpenAI credentials, and PCL execution remains isolated from
the official GPT main session.
